  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Back to Basics - Parliament as a Backbone for the Rule of Law</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Action aims to contribute to reforms in the rule of law sector through supporting the democratic performance of the Parliament in its primary role to uphold the rule of law in the country. Submitted by CRTA with two co-applicants, duration 42 months. Main activities: adjusting existing methodology to work with parliament and citizens; monitoring, analysis and reporting on the work of Parliament; developing Parliament&apos;s rules of procedure; multi-stakeholder conference; advocacy activities including meetings with decision-makers; briefings with international community; meetings with academia and media 4) Outreach including on-line campaign, off-line campaign in local communities; work with media.</narrative>
  </description>
